{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce.</b> We find in every place the expression of עַזּוּת (brazenness) applied to the face, and the expression of קַשְׁיוּת (stubbornness) applied to the neck, which is on the other side from the face. And when he cursed, he cursed only the עַזּוּת of their face and the קַשְׁיוּת of their neck, and he said 'אָרוּר אַפָּם' — and when? 'כִּי עָז,' when it is fierce. And 'עֶבְרָתָם' means the other side of their face, that is, the face; and on the other side is the neck, and regarding the other side, that is, the neck, he said 'כִּי קָשָׁתָה.' And Jacob said that if these two tribes were to remain possessing the trait of brazenness of face and stubbornness of neck, who would be able to stand before them, and they too would be in the uttermost of evil. Therefore 'אֲחַלְּקֵם בְּיַעֲקֹב וַאֲפִיצֵם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל' — that is to say: the greater part of the trait of brazenness of face and of the trait of stubbornness of neck that is in the nature of these two brothers, I divide and disperse among all Israel — כִּי הֵיכֵי דְּלִימְטֵי לְכָל חַד שִׂיבָא מִכָּשׁוֹרָא, that is to say, when it spreads among all Israel it will not reach each individual of Israel except as a small part. And this is what Moses called all Israel 'עַם קְשֵׁה עֹרֶף,' as it says (Exodus 34:9) 'כִּי עַם קְשֵׁה עֹרֶף הוּא.' And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Beitzah 25b) said 'Three are fierce: Israel among the nations,' etc. — because they received the nature of עַזּוּת and קַשְׁיוּת עֹרֶף from Shimon and Levi, for Jacob divided them among all his sons." "Another matter: even though עַזּוּת and קַשְׁיוּת עֹרֶף are bad traits, nevertheless they have an aspect of good, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Avot 5:23) 'הֱוֵי עַז כַּנָּמֵר … לַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹן אָבִיךָ שֶׁבַּשָּׁמַיִם,' and likewise קַשְׁיוּת הָעֹרֶף is good only for Israel, so that they may stand firm in their faith and not turn back for anything to heed the voice of strangers. And this is what Jacob said: 'שֶׁאַפָּם כִּי עָז,' and 'עֶבְרָתָם,' that is, the other side of their face, 'כִּי קָשָׁתָה' — and this is certainly a bad trait. And what is the law — what is to be done with them, to turn them to good? 'אֲחַלְּקֵם בְּיַעֲקֹב וַאֲפִיצֵם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל' — that is to say, I divide and disperse the עַזּוּת and קַשְׁיוּת עֹרֶף to the doers of the deeds of Jacob and Israel, that is, to turn their activity to good as stated. And the reason that Jacob combined them while Moses separated them is because he had already said 'אֲחַלְּקֵם' etc.; therefore Moses was not authorized to rejoin them. Nevertheless he blessed them somewhat in the manner of Jacob's blessing, for he said 'בָּרֵךְ ה׳ חֵילוֹ' (Deuteronomy 33:11), which Onkelos explained as referring to possessions, for Levi had no portion or inheritance except the gifts due him. Thus Jacob said 'אֲחַלְּקֵם בְּיַעֲקֹב' — that is to say, I allot him a portion among all Jacob, for from all Israel they take their share. And even though because of 'כְּלֵי חָמָס מְכֵרֹתֵיהֶם' (Genesis 49:5), that is, to rob the money of the entire city, the judgment is to penalize them so that they all be poor — nevertheless, 'אֲחַלְּקֵם בְּיַעֲקֹב' — to receive their gifts from them, and the tribe of Shimon, 'אֲפִיצֵם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל' — to be scribes and teachers. And therefore Moses hinted at a blessing for Shimon within the blessing of Judah, for from Judah too a tribe of scribes is drawn, as it is written 'וּמְחֹקֵק מִבֵּין רַגְלָיו' (Genesis 49:10), and מְחֹקֵק means a scribe."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase כִּי הֵיכֵי דְּלִימְטֵי לְכָל חַד שִׂיבָא מִכָּשׁוֹרָא is rendered literally in the body of the translation per the instruction to preserve wordplay and observations."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:34.094549459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}